            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> But it's actually split the currently opened window instead of one being highlighted in the Mini.Files window.\r\n> Do we have any way to get the currently selected item to split?\r\n\r\nThis is an example of how to [create mappings to modify target window via split](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e578f353d0b1d9f21a9640458d8e506c0c9acf5e/doc/mini-files.txt#L429) and not how to open file under cursor in a split. After making the split with mapping, open file as usual and it will be opened in the newly created split.\r\n\r\n> Also it would be great if we can specify if the Mini.Files popup should stay or automatically close after the keymap.\r\n\r\nExplorer windows are closed after `MiniFiles.close()` is called or focus is forced outside of them. In turn, `close()` is called after `mappings.close` or `mappings.go_in_plus` is pressed. Other than that, explorer stays open.\r\n\r\nIf you want explorer to be closed in custom mapping, call `close()` explicitly.",
